{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/463425-skein-walking-clarification-needed","id":463425,"title":"Skein-walking clarification needed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-31T06:48:58-07:00","id":463425,"title":"Skein-walking clarification needed","content":"The are some aspects of Skeinwalking I'm not completely sure about, could any of you help me where you think I'm wrong?<br /> <br /> Let's say that I want to travel from source dreamer A to destination dreamer B when they're both asleep.<br /> <br /> There are few possible A-s for me as a Changeling:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Myself.</li> <li>Fetch.</li> <li>Pledge-bound dreamer.</li> <li>Target of Contract of Dream 2 - <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Forging the Dream based on interpretation found in ww forum archive: <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/default0373-11.html?g=posts&amp;m=594276#post594276\" target=\"_blank\">http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/d...276#post594276</a>. </span></span></li> </ol>In cases 1-3 I can predict if a particular dream with an open gate will occur using Oneiroscopy. In cases 2-4 I can use dream-shaping, where 4 is literally like forcing a success, to perform Gate-Shaping.<br /> While there is no doubt that a Lost one might consider Gate-Shaping unethical I wonder about Oneiroscopy. By using a very successful tarot divination I basically force the dream to happen by using my link to the Wyrd. The dream will come next time the subject falls asleep, without my interference there wouldn't be a guarantee that it would happen. In a quantum mechanical sense I collapsed the wave function. On the ethical side it doesn't seem too different from dream-shaping. A Changeling with a little education and relatively high Clarity should be equally haunted by guilt in both cases, if the situation or dream theme wronged the sleeper in any way.<br /> For example if a Lost plans to fight a mind-wrecking Skein-walker that plagues his neighborhood, he needs to perform Oneiroscopy on his pledge-bound dreamer and predict when they will have a thematically linked nightmare, thus inducing it by making divination. By affecting the Skein itself they opened a dangerous gate that can be used by the Skein-walker itself, something even worse might be drawn.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">Now let's consider the destination B. Let's assume that I somehow managed to pass the first Gate from A and I'm traveling through dreamscapes and Skein. How can I be certain that the dreamer B will have this particular dream with an open gate? Should I also make them the target of Oneiroscopy prior to entering the dreams of A? If I'm successful didn't I just make two people's dreamscapes (A and B's) align in skein by playing with Wyrd? It may even affect their fates, to fall asleep in sync so their REM phases overlap. Isn't it a bit like tale-crafting? </span><br /> <br /> How I see it, the shortest and quickest way to get to someone's sleeping mind would be the use of Forging the Dream on both source and destination, ideally a sleeping couple. If you're not a Autumn Court member or their close friend (and thus familiar with secrets of Oneiroscopy) and you don't have the Dreams 2, it would be basically impossible for you to make the A-B journey. Even if you're pledge-bound to some mob boss's lover there wouldn't be a way for you to tell when a passage between the two's dreamscapes will be open. One possibility I see is that you'd need the know about boss's recurring dreams and try to hunt for a Gate in the lover's sleeping mind for it, it might appear one night. Even if you dreamshape the lover's dream you don't have a guarantee that the latter is having this dream or even asleep at that given moment.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5073-casualmoth","name":"CasualMoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5073_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T07:53:35-07:00","id":464666,"title":"","content":"Right I can see that I got carried away and posted a tl;dr topic:<br /> The thing that interests me the most: Is it really possible to get into someone's dreams via Skeinwalking without Oneiroscopy ? The target is someone with whom I don't have a dream-task pledge and I'm not allowed to go in, in a conventional way.<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5073-casualmoth","name":"CasualMoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5073_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T16:23:46-07:00","id":465309,"title":"","content":"You can make a Dream Gate through Dreamshaping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T00:20:59-07:00","id":465757,"title":"","content":"How can you dreamshape if you don't have a pledge of dreamtasking and can't enter someone's dream in the first place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5073-casualmoth","name":"CasualMoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5073_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T07:20:41-07:00","id":466033,"title":"","content":"You go in someone's dream who you can normally, then you dreamshape a gate to another dream.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T08:51:07-07:00","id":466163,"title":"","content":"Or hell, even start from your own dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T11:53:27-07:00","id":466345,"title":"","content":"According to the core rulebook you can't dreamscape your own dreams. But that's not my point. Let's say that an other motley member enters my dreams, we share a dream-pledge. He opens up a gate in my dreams and we enter the Skein. Now here's the tricky part, we want to enter a specific dream of a known person - let's police commissioner's. In order to do it we would need to know his dreams, but we don't. We can only open a gate to Skein and walk randomly, to a random nightmare, random poisoned dream, random memory dream, whatever we aim at.<br /> That's my whole point.<br /> It's impossible to enter dreams of a specific person without Oneiroscopy, by traveling through Skein, based on the rules we currently have. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5073-casualmoth","name":"CasualMoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5073_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T12:07:59-07:00","id":466350,"title":"","content":"You have a person in mind. You pick a direction, and you go. The first dream won't be what you're looking for, but the seventh or so will be. There's a chart somewhere detailing how many dreams are inbetween your starting dream and ending dream. You're overthinking things, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}